<comment datatype='string'>&lt;a href=&quot;/META/NEW-IMAGE?type=EC-NUMBER&amp;object=EC-1.3.8.6&quot;&gt;EC 1.3.8.6, glutaryl-CoA dehydrogenase (ETF)&lt;/a&gt;, which is encoded by the &lt;a href=&quot;/gene?orgid=META&amp;id=G1G01-166&quot;&gt;gcdH&lt;/a&gt; gene, is a key enzyme in the &lt;a href=&quot;/META/NEW-IMAGE?type=PATHWAY&amp;object=PWY-5177&quot;&gt;glutaryl-CoA degradation&lt;/a&gt; pathway.
&lt;p&gt;
Two enzymes in &lt;a href=&quot;/META/NEW-IMAGE?object=TAX-160488&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Pseudomonas putida&lt;/i&gt; KT2440&lt;/a&gt; can act on &lt;a href=&quot;/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=GLUTARATE&quot;&gt;glutarate&lt;/a&gt; - &lt;a href=&quot;/gene?orgid=META&amp;id=G1G01-166&quot;&gt;gcdH&lt;/a&gt;, which encodes &lt;a href=&quot;/META/NEW-IMAGE?type=EC-NUMBER&amp;object=EC-1.3.8.6&quot;&gt;EC 1.3.8.6, glutaryl-CoA dehydrogenase (ETF)&lt;/a&gt;, and &lt;a href=&quot;/gene?orgid=META&amp;id=G1G01-3088&quot;&gt;csiD&lt;/a&gt;, which encodes &lt;a href=&quot;/META/NEW-IMAGE?type=EC-NUMBER&amp;object=EC-1.14.11.64&quot;&gt;EC 1.14.11.64, glutarate dioxygenase&lt;/a&gt;. Inactivation of each gene alone does not result in a strong phenotype. However, inactivation of both genes results in a mutant that is incapable of using &lt;a href=&quot;/compound?orgid=META&amp;id=GLUTARATE&quot;&gt;glutarate&lt;/a&gt; as its sole carbon source [&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pubmed/29844506&quot;&gt;Zhang18b&lt;/a&gt;].</comment>
